 "method": "Renter households paying 50.0 percent or more (B25070_010) divided by renter households for whom the ratio is computed: all renter-occupied units (B25070_001) minus 'not computed' (B25070_011), times 100. 'Not computed' covers units with no cash rent and households with zero or negative income. Margin of error for the denominator is the root-sum-of-squares of the two published margins; the share uses the formula for proportions. Citywide figures are for New York city (place 3651000); peers are matched on place GEOID (state + place FIPS) from data/peers.json; borough figures are the five counties.",
 "caveats": [
  "Gross rent is what the household pays, after any rent subsidy; households in rent-regulated and subsidized apartments are included.",
  "The ACS 1-year 2020 standard tables were never released (the Census Bureau published only experimental estimates because of pandemic data-collection problems), so 2020 is missing from every ACS series.",
  "The 2005 ACS covered only people in households; group quarters (dorms, prisons, nursing homes, shelters) were added in 2006. 2005 values are not strictly comparable to later years.",
  "All ACS figures are survey estimates. moe is the 90 percent margin of error, published by the Census Bureau for single cells and derived with the Bureau's approximation formulas for sums, shares and ratios."
 ]
}
